TU1NZ COMMERCIAL S11.2-R10.1 RECOVERY PREFLIGHT STATE
Date: 2026-09-22

Scope
-----
Read-only final-preflight diagnosis followed by a source-only contract repair.
No S8 start, runtime deployment, evidence mutation, Telegram mutation or S11
activation occurred.

Observed state
--------------
- S8 Telegram was inactive/dead with Result=success, MainPID=0 and NRestarts=0.
- The inactive timestamp followed the R9 fail-closed stop.
- The release-bound polling row retained BOT_POLLER_NOT_RUNNING with an expired
  lease and no recent successful poll.
- S9 health retained exit status 44.
- S7, S8 Landing, S10 WMS and nginx remained active with NRestarts=0.

Root cause
----------
The recovery preflight encoded only the transient failed/start-limit-hit state.
R9's fail-closed handler subsequently stopped S8, which normalised systemd to
inactive/dead with a successful stop result. The safe terminal state therefore
failed a stale preflight assertion even though every release-bound failure
signature remained intact.

Repair contract
---------------
Accept exactly failed/failed/start-limit-hit or inactive/dead/success. Both
states continue to require MainPID=0, NRestarts=0, the exact polling failure
signature, S9 exit 44, healthy unrelated services and GREEN publication
rotation. Every other state fails closed as
S11_2_R10_1_S8_RECOVERY_STATE_DRIFT.
